/*

Azure Subscription Inventory Export

This Bash script generates a CSV inventory of all enabled Azure subscriptions within the authenticated tenant. It uses the Azure CLI to enumerate subscriptions and extracts the Owner value from subscription tags.

The generated report includes:

Subscription Name
Subscription ID
Owner (from the Owner or owner subscription tag)
Report Date

The script automatically:

Verifies that the Azure CLI is installed.
Authenticates the user if no active Azure session exists.
Processes all enabled subscriptions.
Exports the results to a timestamped CSV file.
Displays progress while generating the report.
Prerequisites
Azure CLI 2.x or later
Read access to the target Azure subscriptions
Permission to read subscription tags
Usage
chmod +x export-subscriptions.sh
./export-subscriptions.sh
Output

A timestamped CSV file is created in the current directory:

Azure_Subscriptions_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.csv

Example:

Subscription Name	Subscription ID	Owner	Report Date
Production	xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx	John Smith	2026-07-30
Development	xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx	Platform Team	2026-07-30
Notes
The script first attempts to read the Owner tag and falls back to owner if necessary.
If neither tag exists, the value N/A is written to the report.
Only subscriptions in the Enabled state are included.
The script does not modify any Azure resources; it performs read-only operations.
Typical Use Cases
Azure governance and subscription inventory
Cloud asset management
Cost management ownership validation
Subscription documentation
Security and compliance reporting
Enterprise Azure audits


*/

#!/bin/bash

set -euo pipefail

OUTPUT_FILE="Azure_Subscriptions_$(date +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S).csv"

# Check Azure CLI
if ! command -v az >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "ERROR: Azure CLI is not installed."
    exit 1
fi

# Login if needed
if ! az account show >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "Logging into Azure..."
    az login
fi

echo "Generating report..."

echo "SubscriptionName,SubscriptionId,Owner,ReportDate" > "$OUTPUT_FILE"

az account list \
    --all \
    --query "[?state=='Enabled'].{name:name,id:id}" \
    -o tsv | while IFS=$'\t' read -r SUB_NAME SUB_ID
do
    echo "Processing: $SUB_NAME"

    OWNER=$(az tag list \
        --resource-id "/subscriptions/${SUB_ID}" \
        --query "properties.tags.Owner" \
        -o tsv 2>/dev/null || true)

    if [[ -z "$OWNER" ]]; then
        OWNER=$(az tag list \
            --resource-id "/subscriptions/${SUB_ID}" \
            --query "properties.tags.owner" \
            -o tsv 2>/dev/null || true)
    fi

    [[ -z "$OWNER" ]] && OWNER="N/A"

    echo "\"$SUB_NAME\",\"$SUB_ID\",\"$OWNER\",\"$(date +%F)\"" >> "$OUTPUT_FILE"

done

echo ""
echo "========================================="
echo "Report successfully generated:"
echo "  $OUTPUT_FILE"
echo "========================================="
